Other games offer save points and Nethack doesn't.  The reason takes a
long time to become clear.  When you restore from save you fail to learn
some lesson, and in Nethack it's rarely the lesson you expect.

>> There's also the classic Nethack strategy of - That didn't work in this
>> game.  Time to start a new character and try something else.  Like why I
>> got into that mess in the first place was often about equipment choices
>> five levels up not about details of what I did on that level.
>
> I'm sure that happens to me too, and I'm learning to
> see it.  But I also frequently die to short-term mistakes.

That's the reason.  It's necessary to learn both strategy and tactics. 
Restoring from a save point can teach tactics but it can not teach
strategy.

What it has never taught me is to type slower so I have a low ascension
ratio.

> Does that mean I must always die and start over
